The notification system only supported a global mode toggle (all/team/off) with no way to mute specific teams or individual users. Adds a full settings panel in the profile tab backed by Firebase cross-device sync.

## Notification settings panel (`buildNotifSettingsHtml`)
- Replaces the 3-button mode selector with an expanded section: mode chips + team mute chips + per-user mute toggles
- Team chips turn red when muted; user rows show 🔔/🔕 toggle per online user
- Rendered from `STATE.friends` so the user list reflects who's currently online

## `shouldNotify(friendInfo)` — extended filtering
```js
// Before: only checked notifPref mode
function shouldNotify(friendInfo) {
  if (STATE.notifPref === "off") return false;
  if (STATE.notifPref === "team" && friendInfo.team !== STATE.team) return false;
  return true;
}

// After: also gates on per-team and per-user blocklists
function shouldNotify(friendInfo) {
  const mode = STATE.notifPref;
  if (mode === "off") return false;
  if (mode === "team" && friendInfo.team !== STATE.team) return false;
  if ((STATE.notifSettings.blockedTeams || []).includes(friendInfo.team)) return false;
  if (friendInfo.id && (STATE.notifSettings.blockedUsers || []).includes(friendInfo.id)) return false;
  return true;
}
```
`friendAtCornerAlarm` now delegates entirely to `shouldNotify`.

## Persistence
- `STATE.notifSettings = { blockedTeams[], blockedUsers[] }` loaded from `localStorage` on boot
- Synced to/from `userPrefs/<uid>/notifSettings` in RTDB on login (includes `mode`) for cross-device consistency

## Database rules (`firebase.database.rules.json`)
Added `userPrefs/$uid` — owner read/write, gated on `accessGranted` like other auth-protected paths.

